"""ant-donor-variability: how much do donors (animals in xenografts) differ, per gene and per module (v1, exploratory).

What it does
------------
For every dataset of the facet layer (primary, human post-mortem or xenograft scope, raw counts served, not excluded
by ``facet_exclude``) and every cell type stratum with at least 12 replicates of at least 40 cells, estimates the
between-replicate variance of every well expressed gene and of every module with the split-half covariance estimator
of ``lib/donor_variance.py`` (read its docstring and ``doc/DESIGN_donor_variability.md`` for the method):

  * cells of a replicate are dealt into four random quarters (hash of the cell id and ``--seed``), counts summed per
    quarter, three balanced pairings of quarters form the halves, TMM from the full replicate;
  * ``V_donor``, reliability, donor SD (log2) with bootstrap intervals over replicates;
  * the unexplained variance after nested designs D0 technical block (cells, UMI per cell, genes per cell,
    mitochondrial fraction, ambient score of foreign lineage markers, long gene index, composition PCs), D1 + sex, age, PMI,
    batch, D2 + disease (host genotype for xenografts), D3 + APOE e4, D4 + Braak, F + 3 to 5 latent factors;
  * per-term Shapley (LMG) shares at ``n - p >= 30``; ``excess_z`` (within-unit ranking) at 20 replicates.

Modules: primary variant ``pseudobulk`` (mean log2 CPM of the module genes minus an expression matched control set, from
the same halves and normalisation), secondary ``cell_mean`` (mean of the per-cell scores of ``<stem>.scores.parquet``,
sources geneset and ucell). A module is analysed only in strata of its cell type scope (``lib/celltype_scope.py``).

Replicates are what the dataset's ``replicate_unit`` says: donors for post-mortem tissue, animals for xenografts (there
"donor variability" is between-animal host variability; grafts of one iPSC line have no genetic donor variance). Scopes are
never mixed. Datasets with ``facet_exclude`` are skipped; the ``facet_donor_exclusions`` rule of the ``.md`` is applied.

Inputs: the h5adstore (read only: .md, .h5ad.mus, .duckdb, counts and scores sidecars) and the genesetstore.
Outputs, only under ``<h5adstore>/_facet_tests/<group>/``:
  <stem>.donor_variability.parquet          genes, one row per (stratum, gene)
  <stem>.donor_variability_modules.parquet  modules, one row per (stratum, method, source, catalog, module)
  <stem>.donor_variability_manifest.json    seed, gates, rungs and technical covariates per unit, versions, md_sha256

Usage::

  ant-donor-variability run --db-id G24/MMG [--min-cells 40] [--seed N] [--no-modules]
  ant-donor-variability run --all [--max-load 12]

Run big jobs under ``nice -n 19 ionice -c3 taskset -c ...``.
"""
